 We don't have a working SGEC (Second-Generation Ethernet Controller) 
driver yet, so you won't be able to use this machine with Linux unless you 
can hack up a TURBOchannel configuration with a PMAD-A card.  You are 
welcome to fix the SGEC driver though. :)  The Linux tree is hosted at 
git://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/jbglaw/vax-linux.git -- not 
terribly up to date compared to Linus's tree (complaints to JBG ;) ), but 
still a good starting point.  This is what I've been using for the 
userland porting effort.

 If you'd like to get involved anyhow, then please subscribe to the 
VAX/Linux mailing list.  I'll see if I am able to make this mailing list's 
archive available somehow -- if all else fails, I can recreate one 
anywhere from my personal e-mail archives.

  Maciej



